    "body": "This adds two full runs of one readout over two stock checkpoints. Neither uses weights of our own, so under your entrant rules both are inference techniques.\n\nReadout (both runs): the model's chat template wraps the request (context, question, lettered options), thinking off; the assistant turn starts with \"Answer: (\" and the answer probabilities are the softmax of the option-letter logits at that position, divided by a temperature. One forward pass per request. Options are never shuffled, pruned or truncated. Within one request the temperature never changes the answer. It does change the score in three places where the kit uses the probabilities themselves: ForecastBench scores the probabilities, and ToolRet and BRIGHT rank candidates by probability across chunk requests that have different option counts, so an option-count temperature changes their order. For Gemma-4-31B-it the same weights at T = 1 score 59.11. With the option-count temperature they score 59.84: ToolRet goes from 0.365 to 0.431, BRIGHT from 0.144 to 0.174 and ForecastBench from 0.262 to 0.202. The other 11 benchmarks whose scores changed moved by at most 0.002. Those were argmax flips on near-ties between two server builds; the T = 1 run was served from our earlier commit a2dfb33.\n\n- Gemma-4-31B-it (google/gemma-4-31B-it @ 842da3794eaa0b77d5f08bae87a17459d91ff475, bf16): 132,422 of 132,422 rows ok, Decision Index 59.84. The temperature depends only on the question's number of options n: T(n) = 10.124 \u2212 1.633 ln n (8.99 at 2 options, 6.36 at 10, 1.93 at 151). 29 rows were re-sent once by the kit's resume; their first attempts were HTTP 500s from out-of-memory errors on the server.\n- Qwen3.6-27B (Qwen/Qwen3.6-27B @ 6a9e13bd6fc8f0983b9b99948120bc37f49c13e9, bf16): 132,422 of 132,422 rows ok, Decision Index 55.73. One global temperature, 1.943. The server crashed twice early in the run (out of memory, then a CUDA illegal-address error). The kit's resume re-sent the failed rows: 41,140 rows were sent twice and 86,013 three times. No row needed more than two retries, and no answered row was re-sent.\n\nTemperatures were fitted by NLL on our own training-set rows. The six tasks whose test splits are in the suite were left out: banking77, clinc_oos, mmlu, arc, winogrande and hellaswag. No suite row was used for fitting or for choosing a configuration. The fit records are in the dataset under code/fit/.\n\nHow it was run: the kit's http engine (kit 52a6989, runner sha256 fac268fc\u202658b8) against our server, github.com/Mapika/decider at 7557fe0 plus the serving scripts copied into the dataset under code/. The frozen rows were split round-robin into eight shard files without changing any row, and eight kit runners sent them to one server. Because of that split, each shard's environment.json shows frozen_corpus_sha256 null and a shard rows_path. The shards were merged keeping the last record per run_id, which is what load_results does. The raw per-shard files, including every error record, are under shards/ and re-score to the same scores.json.\n\nHardware and latency: one NVIDIA B300 per run, not the RTX PRO 6000. latency_ms in scores.json is HTTP loopback time with eight concurrent runners against one batching server, so each request includes time queued behind the others. It is not comparable with the other rows. Please re-measure on your hardware or show latency for these rows as not comparable.\n\nThe results dataset is gated on Hugging Face, like surogate's, because it carries the suite's GPQA and HLE text: https://huggingface.co/datasets/Mapika/decision-index-results. Please request access from the dataset page; we approve requests manually.\n\nCapacity limits: none. No request was unsupported or truncated.\n\nQuestion: how do you want two stock models under one readout listed, one row each or one row for the project?\n",
